      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1333404374,
      "text": "Landolphia heudelotii is a climbing shrub or liana that is within the Apocynaceae family, it occurs in the Guinea and Sudan savannahs of West Africa and cultivated for its rubber and edible fruit. It is known as toll or boufembe."
    },
