        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1333404374,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "Wood is used in local carpentry work and making tool handles and doors. A decoction is used to treat diarrhea or intestinal worms in cattle, goat and sheep. Its latex was widely used in Senegal for rubber, and today, it is still used as a rubber substitute to repair bike tubes.",
